# RigIntel core

- Product: private corporate AI platform for one company, domain `rigintel.ai`.
- Canonical git remote: `https://github.com/n8node/aiapp.git`.
- Audience: about 300 employees; design for at least 100 new AI requests/minute.
- Primary language: Russian UI and user messages; code, identifiers, API fields, and technical comments in English.
- Public routing: `/` is WordPress; `/app` is Next.js; `/app/api/v1` is the business API.
- Access is public Internet over HTTPS without VPN. Never rely on network location as authentication.
- Identity: local registration, email verification, login, password reset, sessions, and admin blocking. No SSO/LDAP unless explicitly requested later.
- Tenant model: one company, isolated department workspaces. A user may belong to multiple workspaces.
- Platform administrators may access all workspaces, but privileged reads and mutations are always audited.
- Initial tools: corporate knowledge chat and document reconciliation.
- Supported sources include PDF, scans/images, DOCX, XLSX, 1C, ERP, DMS, mail, and file shares.
- Every external side effect proposed by an agent requires explicit human approval before execution.
- Department managers may request fine-tuning through admin workflows; users never receive shell, Python, CUDA, or raw Studio access.
- Conversation and document retention is configurable by administrators per data category.
- Target host: Ubuntu 24.04, 48 vCPU, 384 GB RAM, 1 TB SSD, 2× NVIDIA A5000 24 GB.
- The two GPUs are separate devices; never assume transparent 48 GB VRAM.
- Production inference has priority. Training is queued for maintenance windows and must not silently degrade online service.
- WordPress/marketing concerns must remain isolated from corporate application data.
